requests.description:
The logged-in user's own notifications, newest first, paginated, plus the current `unreadCount`. Any authenticated role. (Test script saves the first id to `notificationId`.)

### Expected (200)
```json
{
  "success": true,
  "message": "Notifications fetched.",
  "data": {
    "unreadCount": 2,
    "notifications": [
      {
        "id": "...", "type": "assessor_assigned",
        "title": "An assessor was assigned",
        "body": "...", "data": { "programId": "..." },
        "read": false, "read_at": null, "created_at": "..."
      }
    ]
  },
  "meta": { "page": 1, "limit": 20, "total": 2, "totalPages": 1 }
}
```

**Notification types:** `new_program_available`, `enrolled_in_program`, `assessor_assigned`, `assessor_visit_started`, `assessment_submitted`.

**Realtime:** the server also pushes `notification:new` and `notification:unread_count` over socket.io to the user's room - the bell updates without a refresh.
